  "summary": "Full assessment of all 1,105 English/Vietnamese passages: Chapters I–XXXIX, from the parrot on the Grand Isle porch to the last paragraph. The first reviews scored 8.475, 8.43, 8.30 and 8.36 across four ranges and found nine majors (a sister placed in the wrong order, a misread idiom, loosely rendered phrases and an unmotivated shift in how Edna is named); the findings were applied with a naturalness pass and fresh separate-context reviews followed, which found one more major (the midday meal rendered as an evening meal) that was corrected. The last fresh reviews scored 8.80 (units 1–252), 8.725 (253–545), 8.65 (546–827) and 8.80 (828–1105) with no major or critical finding, and the remaining minor points were applied. The final score is taken from the weakest range, 8.65 on the half-point scale, above the unchanged 8.6 threshold. No unresolved major or critical issue remains.",
